# Architecture (DDD + clean boundaries)

- **Presentation:** `app/**`, `components/**` — UI, composition, and local UI state. Avoid embedding domain rules that belong in application services.
- **Application / domain services:** `lib/*.ts` modules (e.g. `buddies.ts`, `join-requests.ts`) — orchestrate use-cases, map DTOs, call Firebase or HTTPS callables. Prefer **one capability per file** over a generic “utils” dump.
- **Domain types:** `types/**` — shared shapes; keep Firestore-specific types thin or in `types/io2026.ts` style.
- **Configuration:** `lib/constants.ts`, `lib/hackathon-collections.ts` — collection names and env switches; do not hardcode collection strings in new code.
- **Data access target:** **No new** direct `firebase/firestore` or `firebase/storage` imports in `components/**`. Prefer `lib/<domain>.ts`, Route Handlers, or **HTTPS Callable** Cloud Functions for privileged writes. **Legacy:** existing pages/components still use the client SDK behind security rules — migrate when touching that area, not drive-by refactors.
- **DDD hint:** name modules after **verbs/use-cases** or **bounded contexts** (e.g. `join-requests`, `bookmarks`), not after frameworks.
- **Reusable admin UI:** `components/admin/*` for dialogs and badges; list/query logic in `lib/admin-users.ts` (or sibling domain modules).
- **UI copy:** do not display raw Firestore collection names or secrets to end users.
